          "text": "Description: On February 20, 2011, at 21:05, a driver observed a green \"fluorescent\" light moving across the sky and splitting into three spheres before disappearing. The described observation resembles a fairly classic meteor: green light, straight trajectory, trail, lasting a few seconds. Note here a fragmentation that is not systematic. The object causing this phenomenon could be a small satellite debris, but more likely of natural origin (meteorite).",
